biolink:DiseaseToDiseaseAssociation a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "An association between two diseases. Captures clinical or biological relationships such as comorbidity, sequela, post-infectious complication, shared susceptibility, or differential diagnosis. The precise relationship is carried by the predicate (e.g. ``associated with``, ``contributes to``, ``risk affected by``, ``temporally related to``); use this class whenever both ends of the association are diseases, rather than the more specific ``disease to phenotypic feature association`` (which forces the object to be a phenotypic feature) or a generic ``association``." ;
	sh:closed true ;
