	sh:description "HGVS syntax refers to the specific rules and conventions used by the Human Variant Nomenclature Committee to describe the location and change in DNA, RNA, and protein sequence variants.  This slot is used to capture all the different forms of HGVS nomenclature that may be used to describe a sequence variant, including genomic, transcript, and protein HGVS expressions/nomenclatures and is thus multivalued." ;
