_:c14n2830 sh:class biolink:QuantityValue ;
	sh:description "In the context of molecular interactions and drug discovery, pXC50 is a generic, base 10 negative logarithmic measure of compound potency that unifies different types of half‑maximal concentration values into a single notation, where XC50 means “the concentration at which 50% of the maximal effect is observed”, and X is a placeholder for the type of effect being measured (e.g., inhibition or activation). The X in pXC50 is intentionally generic and can represent different assay endpoints." ;
	sh:maxCount 1 ;
	sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
	sh:order 5 ;
	sh:path biolink:pXC50 .
