_:c14n6749 sh:description "Predicate to be used in an association when subject and object qualifiers are present and the full reading of the statement requires a qualification to the predicate in use in order to refine or increase the specificity of the full statement reading.  Has a value from the Biolink 'related_to' hierarchy, for example, biolink:related_to, biolink:causes, biolink:treats This qualifier holds a relationship to be used instead of that expressed by the primary predicate, in a ‘full statement’ reading of the association, where qualifier-based semantics are included. This is necessary only in cases where the primary predicate does not work in a full statement reading." ;
